{
  "name": "248. MCP library installed flag survives a client rename (mcp library installed) (#8548)",
  "description": "Regression for #8548. The MCP Library page decided which catalog entries were installed in the browser, from one page (100) of MCP clients, matching only by connection URL or by a client name equal to the sanitized entry name. Clients past the first 100 were never considered, and a client renamed after install (or a stdio entry, which has no URL) showed as not installed.\n\nGET /api/mcp/library now returns `installed` on every entry, computed server-side over every MCP client row. A client matches by the proposed install name, by its endpoint slug (derived from that name at create and immutable, so it survives a rename), by the http/sse URL, or by stdio command plus args.\n\nThe cases publish a custom library entry, create an openapi-type client (no upstream MCP server needed) under the name the install flow proposes, rename it, and assert the entry still reports installed. After the client is deleted the entry must report not installed. Pre-fix the field is absent, so the rename assertion fails.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "openai mcp-library-installed publish a custom library entry - #8548",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Run-unique identity (timestamp plus a random suffix): parallel runs never collide.",
              "var run = Date.now() + '-' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('libInstalledEntryName', 'harness-lib-installed-' + run);",
              "// The install flow proposes the entry name with every run of characters outside [A-Za-z0-9_] turned into '_'.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('libInstalledClientName', 'harness_lib_installed_' + run.replace('-', '_'));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('libInstalledRenamed', 'harness_lib_renamed_' + run.replace('-', '_'));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('libInstalledClientId', 'harness-lib-installed-' + run);",
              "// A run that stopped before its cleanup leaves rows behind. Remove this folder's own leftovers once they are over an hour old.",
              "var cutoff = Date.now() - 3600000;",
              "var base = pm.variables.get('baseUrl');",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: base + '/api/mcp/library?search=harness-lib-installed-&limit=100', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('leftover library entries listed', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null);",
              "    pm.expect(res.code, res.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  });",
              "  if (err || res.code !== 200) { return; }",
              "  (res.json().servers || []).forEach(function (s) {",
              "    var m = /^harness-lib-installed-(\\d{13})-/.exec(s.name || '');",
              "    if (!m || Number(m[1]) >= cutoff) { return; }",
              "    pm.sendRequest({ url: base + '/api/mcp/library/' + s.id, method: 'DELETE' }, function (derr, dres) {",
              "      pm.test('leftover library entry ' + s.name + ' removed', function () {",
              "        pm.expect(derr, String(derr)).to.equal(null);",
              "        pm.expect(dres.code === 200 || dres.code === 404, 'status ' + dres.code + ': ' + dres.text()).to.equal(true);",
              "      });",
              "    });",
              "  });",
              "});",
              "['harness_lib_installed_', 'harness_lib_renamed_'].forEach(function (prefix) {",
              "  pm.sendRequest({ url: base + '/api/mcp/clients?search=' + prefix + '&limit=100', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "    pm.test('leftover ' + prefix + ' clients listed', function () {",
              "      pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null);",
              "      pm.expect(res.code, res.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "    });",
              "    if (err || res.code !== 200) { return; }",
              "    (res.json().clients || []).forEach(function (c) {",
              "      var name = (c.config && c.config.name) || '';",
              "      var m = new RegExp('^' + prefix + '(\\\\d{13})_').exec(name);",
              "      if (!m || Number(m[1]) >= cutoff) { return; }",
              "      pm.sendRequest({ url: base + '/api/mcp/client/' + encodeURIComponent(c.config.client_id), method: 'DELETE' }, function (derr, dres) {",
              "        pm.test('leftover client ' + name + ' removed', function () {",
              "          pm.expect(derr, String(derr)).to.equal(null);",
              "          var gone = dres.code === 500 && dres.text().indexOf('not found') !== -1;",
              "          pm.expect(dres.code === 200 || gone, 'status ' + dres.code + ': ' + dres.text()).to.equal(true);",
              "        });",
              "      });",
              "    });",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('custom library entry is published', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  var entry = (pm.response.json() || {}).entry || {};",
              "  pm.expect(entry.id, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('number');",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('libInstalledEntryId', String(entry.id));",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"{{libInstalledEntryName}}\",\n  \"description\": \"Harness fixture for the installed flag\",\n  \"connection_type\": \"http\",\n  \"connection_url\": \"https://harness-lib-installed.invalid/mcp\",\n  \"auth_type\": \"none\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/mcp/library",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "mcp",
            "library"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
